        "nobel_worthiness": "Geometric and topological phases reshaped quantum mechanics and became indispensable across atomic, condensed-matter, and optical physics.",
        "attribution": "Aharonov and Bohm identified a striking phase effect with deep physical consequences; Berry generalized geometric phase for adiabatic quantum evolution. The listed pair captures two foundational contributions, though the broader development involved many others.",
        "maturity": "These effects have been confirmed repeatedly and underpin well-established theory and experiments.",
