      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Dynamical mean-field theory gave condensed-matter physics a powerful framework for strongly correlated electrons and transformed the study of Mott transitions and correlated materials.",
        "attribution": "Georges, Vollhardt, and Kotliar were central to developing the framework and establishing its applications; credit is appropriately shared among theorists who connected and advanced its key formulations.",
        "maturity": "The theory has been applied and refined for decades, with broad use alongside experiments on correlated materials.",
