      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Spin ice revealed a highly unusual collective state in real crystals, where fractionalized excitations behave in important ways like magnetic monopoles and illuminate frustrated magnetism.",
        "attribution": "Castelnovo, Moessner, and Bramwell made the pivotal theoretical and experimental contributions that connected spin-ice physics to emergent monopole behavior.",
        "maturity": "The spin-ice state and its characteristic excitations are supported by extensive experimental and theoretical work.",
